sking me to forecast outcomes for the incomplete experiments. Looking at the full list of experiments in the registry, I see that only `diagnostic-rerepair` and `swebench-pertest-data` are marked as planned in the experiment_plan. However, since the user is asking about the median tier's assumptions, I should also include predictions for the RUNNING/PREPARING DeepSeek experiments that are central to that definition, treating them as forward-looking scenarios alongside the strictly planned ones. I need to clarify what the user is actually asking for—they want the planned experiments from the experiment_plan specifically. But looking at the median tier's predictions, the RUNNING and PREPARING DeepSeek experiments are really the core validation work that the median tier makes claims about, so I should include those as well since they're incomplete and central to the overall plan.\n\nFor diagnostic-rerepair, the median tier predicts it stays at the current negative results with no meaningful improvement from per-test diagnostic information. For swebench-pertest-data, it's a data construction task that should complete successfully but won't shift the experimental conclusions. Now looking at deepseek-cls-repo which is currently running—the median tier expects it to land in the 70-78% accuracy range, which would be 5-12 percentage points below Qwen's best performance on repo-level classification.\n\nFor deepseek-cwm-repo, I'm expecting around 15-40% unparseable cases with the parseable subset reaching 60-72% accuracy, maintaining that same 5-12pp gap from the classification baseline. The trajectory-based repo experiment won't finish in time for the May 25 deadline. On the function-level side, there are three deepseek trajectory experiments at various stages—one analyzing results, one that failed during preparation, and another still in the queue.\n\nLooking at the completed function-level data, the classification and CWM variants are showing interesting patterns: the base models have a 1.16pp gap favoring classification, which fits within the expected [-0.5, 1.5] range, but the s123 variants flip this with CWM actually outperforming classification by 1.11pp.\n\nFor the trajectory variant, I'm seeing a larger gap between classification and trajectory approaches—around 3.69pp on seed42 and 1.69pp on s123, averaging roughly 2.7pp, which sits comfortably within the [2, 5] target range.\n\nNow I need to construct the YAML output covering all planned experiments from the plan plus the key incomplete ones that matter for the median tier definition. The plan itself only marks two as \"planned,\" but I should include the running and preparing experiments since they're central to the median tier claims.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31771,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31771},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2d7180c-b21d-4a12-a938-cc2a4c8f76d9","uuid":"b9a7d4ff-f4c3-4d3c-ab0e-2f4cb0d252fd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PYt5Bjv3ML6iP6bFHRn3Za","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: \"C1 弱化为 model-dependent advantage；DeepSeek 作为 directionally consistent secondary evidence；C2 限定 Qwen-validated；Re-repair 列为 limitation/future work。目标 EMNLP Findings。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"给 repair agent 提供 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，对比 200 instances resolve rate\"\n    expected_results:\n      control_resolve_rate: 0.215\n      cls_diag_resolve_rate: 0.225\n      oracle_diag_resolve_rate: 0.285\n      random_diag_resolve_rate: 0.175\n      delta_cls_vs_control_pp: 1.0\n      delta_oracle_vs_control_pp: 7.0\n      p_value_cls_vs_control: 0.62\n      n_instances: 200\n      n_repair_attempts_per_instance: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase0 已证实 cls_diag (0.818) ≈ control (0.82) 无显著差异。\n      Median 档假设 re-repair 停留在负面结果：per-test diagnostic 信息虽然理论上可指导修复方向，\n      但当前 classifier 精度不足以可靠区分 failing tests（fail_precision=82.75%，约 17% 假阳性），\n      repair agent 会被误导性诊断分散注意力。Oracle diag 有效（+7pp）说明问题不在 repair agent 能力，\n      而在 verifier 精度不够。200 instances 下 1pp 差异 (p=0.62) 统计不显著，\n      无法支撑 downstream impact claim。此结果迫使论文将 diagnostic utility 限定为 \"potential\" 而非 \"demonstrated\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Re-repair resolve rates by condition (control / cls-diag / oracle-diag / random-diag)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: resolve rate ± 95% CI across 4 conditions, showing oracle-diag significantly above control but cls-diag overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Re-repair 实验证实当前 verifier 精度下 per-test diagnostic 不足以转化为下游收益。\n      Oracle 条件有效说明方向正确但需更高精度。论文中作为 limitation 讨论：\n      \"per-test predictions enable diagnostic granularity in principle; downstream utility \n      requires verifier precision exceeding ~90% (oracle analysis suggests +7pp resolve rate \n      is achievable with perfect predictions)\"。列为 future work。\n\n  - name: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation 提取 SWE-bench Verified per-test labels，构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_extraction: 438\n      failed_docker: 62\n      fail_rate_docker_pct: 12.4\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_test_pairs: 87600\n      pass_ratio: 0.73\n      fail_ratio: 0.27\n      median_tests_per_instance: 12\n      mean_code_length_tokens: 3800\n      processing_time_hours: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      SWE-bench Verified 有 500 instances，Docker 基础设施通常有 10-15% 环境构建失败率\n      （依赖版本冲突、过时 apt 源等）。Per-test label 提取本身是确定性的（运行 pytest 收集结果），\n      主要风险在 Docker 环境搭建。438 instances × 16 candidates = 7008 patch-level 样本，\n      每个展开为约 12 tests = ~87K test-level pairs。pass/fail 比例约 73/27 与已观测 majority_baseline=72.96% 一致。\n      此数据集是 repo-level training 的基础。Median 档下数据成功构建，但训练结果有限（见 deepseek-cls-repo）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Dataset statistics (instances, candidates, test pairs, class distribution)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: tests-per-instance distribution showing right-skewed with median=12\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功，为 repo-level 实验提供训练/评估数据。\n      作为 resource contribution 可在 paper 中强调。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training (DeepSeek variant)\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite-Base 在 repo-level per-test classification 上的 fine-tune\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy_pct: 74.2\n      f1_macro: 67.8\n      f1_pass: 82.5\n      f1_fail: 53.1\n      precision_fail: 62.3\n      recall_fail: 46.4\n      unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 1.24\n      gap_vs_qwen4b_best_pp: -8.15  # vs cls4b-v5 ckpt4600 val=90.07%\n      gap_vs_qwen8b_best_pp: -10.5  # vs cls8b-seed123 ckpt3000 val=88.69%\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n      training_time_sec: 18000\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3 系列在 repo-level CLS 上最佳成绩为 4B:90.07%(val)/83.63%(test)，8B:88.69%(val)/84.79%(test)。\n      Median 档假设 DeepSeek repo CLS 在 70-78% 区间。DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite（15.7B 但 active 2.4B MoE）\n      在 func-level 已表现出比 Qwen3 低约 1-3pp 的基线（86.93% vs Qwen 88.41% mean），\n      但 repo-level 差距会放大：(1) DeepSeek 的 tokenizer 对 repo-level 长上下文效率较低，\n      (2) MoE 架构在 LoRA fine-tune 下 expert routing 适应较慢，\n      (3) repo-level 任务需要跨文件理解，DeepSeek 在此类 reasoning 上弱于 Qwen3。\n      5-12pp 差距反映了架构适配度差异而非训练数据问题。74.2% 刚过 majority baseline，\n      说明模型学到了信号但 capacity 不足以稳定泛化。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-model repo-level CLS comparison (Qwen-4B / Qwen-8B / DeepSeek)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: accuracy by model showing consistent ranking Qwen8B > Qwen4B > DeepSeek\"\n    analysis: >\n      DeepSeek repo CLS 方向性一致（above majority baseline）但幅度显著低于 Qwen。\n      论文中作为 \"directionally consistent secondary evidence\" 呈现：\n      同一 formulation 在不同 architecture 上都能学到 signal，但 effect size 受 model capacity 调制。\n      支撑 model-dependent caveat in C1。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training (DeepSeek CWM variant)\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite-Base 在 repo-level CWM generation 上的 fine-tune\"\n    expected_results:\n      overall_accuracy_pct: 62.8\n      parseable_rate_pct: 72.0\n      unparseable_pct: 28.0\n      parseable_subset_accuracy_pct: 66.3\n      f1_macro: 48.2\n      f1_pass: 74.6\n      f1_fail: 21.8\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -10.16\n      cls_cwm_gap_pp: 11.4  # 74.2 - 62.8\n      qwen_cwm_repo_comparison: \"Qwen repo CWM unparseable 53-93%; DeepSeek 28% much better\"\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      training_time_sec: 22000\n      gen_length_mean: 2800\n      gen_length_median: 2100\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：DeepSeek repo CWM unparseable 15-40%，parseable 子集精度 60-72%。\n      对比 Qwen repo CWM（v10: 93% unparseable; v12: 53.7%），DeepSeek 的 code generation 能力\n      更强（DeepSeek-Coder 系列专为代码生成优化），因此 format compliance 更好（28% unparseable vs Qwen 53-93%）。\n      但 parseable 子集精度仍受限于 token-budget exhaustion：repo-level 输出通常需要 2000+ tokens，\n      即使格式正确，内容也容易出现 string-value prediction errors。\n      CLS-CWM gap 缩小至 11.4pp（vs Qwen 的 15+pp），因为 DeepSeek 的 generation quality \n      部分抵消了 CWM 的固有劣势。这一结果使 C1 的 claim 必须加 model-dependent caveat：\n      \"CLS advantage magnitude varies with model architecture (5-12pp for DeepSeek vs 15+pp for Qwen)\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Repo-level CWM cross-model comparison (parseability, accuracy, CLS gap)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: parseable vs unparseable predictions by model\"\n      - \"Scatter: CLS-CWM gap (y) vs unparseable rate (x) across models, showing positive correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      DeepSeek CWM 的低 unparseable rate 是意外发现——说明 format compliance 是 model-dependent，\n      不能一概而论 \"CWM fails at repo-level\"。但 parseable subset accuracy 仍低于 CLS，\n      维持了 \"CLS provides more robust formulation\" 的方向性结论。\n      Gap 缩小（11.4pp vs Qwen 15+pp）要求论文弱化 universal claim，改为 architecture-modulated。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-repo\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level trajectory-level fine-tune (与 CLS 对比支撑 C2 跨模型)\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_COMPLETED\"\n      reason: \"ARR May 25 deadline; training infrastructure conflict with cls-repo/cwm-repo\"\n      partial_data_available: false\n      estimated_completion: \"2026-06-01\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档明确假设 DeepSeek TRAJ repo 未能在 ARR May 25 前完成。\n      原因：(1) deepseek-cls-repo 和 deepseek-cwm-repo 占用全部 GPU 资源至 5月18-20日，\n      (2) TRAJ 数据准备需要 variant-level aggregation 逻辑重写适配 DeepSeek tokenizer，\n      (3) 即使立即开始训练也需 3-5 天完成 training + evaluation sweep。\n      这意味着 C2 (CLS≈TRAJ equivalence) 无法跨模型验证，只能基于 Qwen 5-seed TOST p=0.007。\n      论文必须承认这是 generalization limitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      缺失 DeepSeek TRAJ repo 数据使 C2 限定为 \"validated within Qwen architecture\"。\n      Reviewer 大概率会指出这一点并要求补充实验。EMNLP Findings 可能接受 single-model validation\n      如果 effect size 和 statistical rigor 足够强（TOST p=0.007, 5 seeds, clustered bootstrap）。\n      Main track 概率低。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-repo-s123\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level TRAJ seed123 variant\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_COMPLETED\"\n      reason: \"同 deepseek-traj-repo，资源和时间约束\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 deepseek-traj-repo 相同的阻塞因素。Median 档下两个 TRAJ repo 实验都未完成。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"同上。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-fixed (func-level TRAJ evaluation fix)\"\n    description: \"修复 DeepSeek func-level TRAJ 评估中的 data leakage / evaluation bug\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"FAILED_TO_RESOLVE\"\n      reason: \"evaluation pipeline bug 无法在 deadline 前修复\"\n      fallback_used: true\n      fallback_metric_source: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2 (unfixed but directionally valid)\"\n      fallback_accuracy: 0.8324\n      cls_traj_gap_pp: 3.69  # 86.93 - 83.24\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 fix 版本因 pipeline 问题失败，但 unfixed 版本（deepseek-traj-func-v2: 83.24%）\n      已有方向性结论。CLS (86.93%) vs TRAJ (83.24%) gap = 3.69pp，在 [2, 5] 范围内。\n      论文采用 unfixed 数据并标注 caveat：\"evaluation uses standard train/test split; \n      per-test leakage analysis pending\"。这是 acceptable 但 reviewer 可能质疑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek func-level three-format comparison (CLS / CWM / TRAJ)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      使用现有 deepseek-traj-func-v2 数据，CLS>TRAJ gap (3.69pp) 作为 suggestive evidence。\n      Seed123: CLS 86.77% vs TRAJ 85.08% = 1.69pp gap。\n      Mean gap: ~2.7pp，在 median 档 [2,5] 范围内但偏下限。\n      论文措辞：\"DeepSeek func-level results suggest CLS≥TRAJ (mean gap 2.7pp, N=2 seeds), \n      though insufficient seeds preclude formal equivalence/superiority testing\"。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-s123-fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-s123-fixed\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek func TRAJ seed123 修复版\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"FAILED_TO_RESOLVE\"\n      reason: \"同 v2-fixed\"\n      fallback_accuracy: 0.8508\n      cls_traj_gap_s123_pp: 1.69  # 86.77 - 85.08\n    result_rationale: >\n      同上。Seed123 unfixed 数据表明 gap 更小 (1.69pp)，增加了结论的不确定性。\n      两个 seed 的 gap 差异 (3.69 vs 1.69) 暗示高方差，进一步支撑 median 档\n      \"仅作 suggestive evidence\" 的定位。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"纳入 seed123 unfixed 数据后 mean gap 降至 2.7pp，方差较大。\"\n```\n\n**关键 median 档叙事总结**：\n\n- **C1**：Qwen 8B CLS-CWM gap = 2.81pp (已验证)；DeepSeek repo gap ~11.4pp 方向一致但因 architecture 差异 CWM parseability 更好，gap 缩小。论文弱化为 \"advantage magnitude modulated by architecture\"。\n- **C2**：仅 Qwen 5-seed TOST p=0.007 standalone。DeepSeek func CLS≥TRAJ (mean 2.7pp) 作为 suggestive evidence，repo-level 缺失。\n- **C3**：不受影响（纯 oracle 分析，model-agnostic）。\n- **Re-repair**：negative，列为 future work。\n- **Critical reviewer concerns**：3/4 addressed（addressed: novelty via scaling + cross-model direction; generalization via DeepSeek secondary evidence; per-test utility via oracle analysis。NOT addressed: downstream impact 仅有 phase0 negative）。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31771,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31771},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2d7180c-b21d-4a12-a938-cc2a4c8f76d9","uuid":"a0863f0d-6fb4-462f-aa36-9dcf9c93bb6b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":157571,"duration_api_ms":159181,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: \"C1 弱化为 model-dependent advantage；DeepSeek 作为 directionally consistent secondary evidence；C2 限定 Qwen-validated；Re-repair 列为 limitation/future work。目标 EMNLP Findings。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"给 repair agent 提供 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，对比 200 instances resolve rate\"\n    expected_results:\n      control_resolve_rate: 0.215\n      cls_diag_resolve_rate: 0.225\n      oracle_diag_resolve_rate: 0.285\n      random_diag_resolve_rate: 0.175\n      delta_cls_vs_control_pp: 1.0\n      delta_oracle_vs_control_pp: 7.0\n      p_value_cls_vs_control: 0.62\n      n_instances: 200\n      n_repair_attempts_per_instance: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase0 已证实 cls_diag (0.818) ≈ control (0.82) 无显著差异。\n      Median 档假设 re-repair 停留在负面结果：per-test diagnostic 信息虽然理论上可指导修复方向，\n      但当前 classifier 精度不足以可靠区分 failing tests（fail_precision=82.75%，约 17% 假阳性），\n      repair agent 会被误导性诊断分散注意力。Oracle diag 有效（+7pp）说明问题不在 repair agent 能力，\n      而在 verifier 精度不够。200 instances 下 1pp 差异 (p=0.62) 统计不显著，\n      无法支撑 downstream impact claim。此结果迫使论文将 diagnostic utility 限定为 \"potential\" 而非 \"demonstrated\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Re-repair resolve rates by condition (control / cls-diag / oracle-diag / random-diag)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: resolve rate ± 95% CI across 4 conditions, showing oracle-diag significantly above control but cls-diag overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Re-repair 实验证实当前 verifier 精度下 per-test diagnostic 不足以转化为下游收益。\n      Oracle 条件有效说明方向正确但需更高精度。论文中作为 limitation 讨论：\n      \"per-test predictions enable diagnostic granularity in principle; downstream utility \n      requires verifier precision exceeding ~90% (oracle analysis suggests +7pp resolve rate \n      is achievable with perfect predictions)\"。列为 future work。\n\n  - name: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation 提取 SWE-bench Verified per-test labels，构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_extraction: 438\n      failed_docker: 62\n      fail_rate_docker_pct: 12.4\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_test_pairs: 87600\n      pass_ratio: 0.73\n      fail_ratio: 0.27\n      median_tests_per_instance: 12\n      mean_code_length_tokens: 3800\n      processing_time_hours: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      SWE-bench Verified 有 500 instances，Docker 基础设施通常有 10-15% 环境构建失败率\n      （依赖版本冲突、过时 apt 源等）。Per-test label 提取本身是确定性的（运行 pytest 收集结果），\n      主要风险在 Docker 环境搭建。438 instances × 16 candidates = 7008 patch-level 样本，\n      每个展开为约 12 tests = ~87K test-level pairs。pass/fail 比例约 73/27 与已观测 majority_baseline=72.96% 一致。\n      此数据集是 repo-level training 的基础。Median 档下数据成功构建，但训练结果有限（见 deepseek-cls-repo）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Dataset statistics (instances, candidates, test pairs, class distribution)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: tests-per-instance distribution showing right-skewed with median=12\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功，为 repo-level 实验提供训练/评估数据。\n      作为 resource contribution 可在 paper 中强调。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training (DeepSeek variant)\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite-Base 在 repo-level per-test classification 上的 fine-tune\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy_pct: 74.2\n      f1_macro: 67.8\n      f1_pass: 82.5\n      f1_fail: 53.1\n      precision_fail: 62.3\n      recall_fail: 46.4\n      unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 1.24\n      gap_vs_qwen4b_best_pp: -8.15  # vs cls4b-v5 ckpt4600 val=90.07%\n      gap_vs_qwen8b_best_pp: -10.5  # vs cls8b-seed123 ckpt3000 val=88.69%\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n      training_time_sec: 18000\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3 系列在 repo-level CLS 上最佳成绩为 4B:90.07%(val)/83.63%(test)，8B:88.69%(val)/84.79%(test)。\n      Median 档假设 DeepSeek repo CLS 在 70-78% 区间。DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite（15.7B 但 active 2.4B MoE）\n      在 func-level 已表现出比 Qwen3 低约 1-3pp 的基线（86.93% vs Qwen 88.41% mean），\n      但 repo-level 差距会放大：(1) DeepSeek 的 tokenizer 对 repo-level 长上下文效率较低，\n      (2) MoE 架构在 LoRA fine-tune 下 expert routing 适应较慢，\n      (3) repo-level 任务需要跨文件理解，DeepSeek 在此类 reasoning 上弱于 Qwen3。\n      5-12pp 差距反映了架构适配度差异而非训练数据问题。74.2% 刚过 majority baseline，\n      说明模型学到了信号但 capacity 不足以稳定泛化。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-model repo-level CLS comparison (Qwen-4B / Qwen-8B / DeepSeek)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: accuracy by model showing consistent ranking Qwen8B > Qwen4B > DeepSeek\"\n    analysis: >\n      DeepSeek repo CLS 方向性一致（above majority baseline）但幅度显著低于 Qwen。\n      论文中作为 \"directionally consistent secondary evidence\" 呈现：\n      同一 formulation 在不同 architecture 上都能学到 signal，但 effect size 受 model capacity 调制。\n      支撑 model-dependent caveat in C1。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training (DeepSeek CWM variant)\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite-Base 在 repo-level CWM generation 上的 fine-tune\"\n    expected_results:\n      overall_accuracy_pct: 62.8\n      parseable_rate_pct: 72.0\n      unparseable_pct: 28.0\n      parseable_subset_accuracy_pct: 66.3\n      f1_macro: 48.2\n      f1_pass: 74.6\n      f1_fail: 21.8\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -10.16\n      cls_cwm_gap_pp: 11.4  # 74.2 - 62.8\n      qwen_cwm_repo_comparison: \"Qwen repo CWM unparseable 53-93%; DeepSeek 28% much better\"\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      training_time_sec: 22000\n      gen_length_mean: 2800\n      gen_length_median: 2100\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：DeepSeek repo CWM unparseable 15-40%，parseable 子集精度 60-72%。\n      对比 Qwen repo CWM（v10: 93% unparseable; v12: 53.7%），DeepSeek 的 code generation 能力\n      更强（DeepSeek-Coder 系列专为代码生成优化），因此 format compliance 更好（28% unparseable vs Qwen 53-93%）。\n      但 parseable 子集精度仍受限于 token-budget exhaustion：repo-level 输出通常需要 2000+ tokens，\n      即使格式正确，内容也容易出现 string-value prediction errors。\n      CLS-CWM gap 缩小至 11.4pp（vs Qwen 的 15+pp），因为 DeepSeek 的 generation quality \n      部分抵消了 CWM 的固有劣势。这一结果使 C1 的 claim 必须加 model-dependent caveat：\n      \"CLS advantage magnitude varies with model architecture (5-12pp for DeepSeek vs 15+pp for Qwen)\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Repo-level CWM cross-model comparison (parseability, accuracy, CLS gap)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: parseable vs unparseable predictions by model\"\n      - \"Scatter: CLS-CWM gap (y) vs unparseable rate (x) across models, showing positive correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      DeepSeek CWM 的低 unparseable rate 是意外发现——说明 format compliance 是 model-dependent，\n      不能一概而论 \"CWM fails at repo-level\"。但 parseable subset accuracy 仍低于 CLS，\n      维持了 \"CLS provides more robust formulation\" 的方向性结论。\n      Gap 缩小（11.4pp vs Qwen 15+pp）要求论文弱化 universal claim，改为 architecture-modulated。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-repo\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level trajectory-level fine-tune (与 CLS 对比支撑 C2 跨模型)\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_COMPLETED\"\n      reason: \"ARR May 25 deadline; training infrastructure conflict with cls-repo/cwm-repo\"\n      partial_data_available: false\n      estimated_completion: \"2026-06-01\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档明确假设 DeepSeek TRAJ repo 未能在 ARR May 25 前完成。\n      原因：(1) deepseek-cls-repo 和 deepseek-cwm-repo 占用全部 GPU 资源至 5月18-20日，\n      (2) TRAJ 数据准备需要 variant-level aggregation 逻辑重写适配 DeepSeek tokenizer，\n      (3) 即使立即开始训练也需 3-5 天完成 training + evaluation sweep。\n      这意味着 C2 (CLS≈TRAJ equivalence) 无法跨模型验证，只能基于 Qwen 5-seed TOST p=0.007。\n      论文必须承认这是 generalization limitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      缺失 DeepSeek TRAJ repo 数据使 C2 限定为 \"validated within Qwen architecture\"。\n      Reviewer 大概率会指出这一点并要求补充实验。EMNLP Findings 可能接受 single-model validation\n      如果 effect size 和 statistical rigor 足够强（TOST p=0.007, 5 seeds, clustered bootstrap）。\n      Main track 概率低。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-repo-s123\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level TRAJ seed123 variant\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_COMPLETED\"\n      reason: \"同 deepseek-traj-repo，资源和时间约束\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 deepseek-traj-repo 相同的阻塞因素。Median 档下两个 TRAJ repo 实验都未完成。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"同上。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-fixed (func-level TRAJ evaluation fix)\"\n    description: \"修复 DeepSeek func-level TRAJ 评估中的 data leakage / evaluation bug\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"FAILED_TO_RESOLVE\"\n      reason: \"evaluation pipeline bug 无法在 deadline 前修复\"\n      fallback_used: true\n      fallback_metric_source: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2 (unfixed but directionally valid)\"\n      fallback_accuracy: 0.8324\n      cls_traj_gap_pp: 3.69  # 86.93 - 83.24\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 fix 版本因 pipeline 问题失败，但 unfixed 版本（deepseek-traj-func-v2: 83.24%）\n      已有方向性结论。CLS (86.93%) vs TRAJ (83.24%) gap = 3.69pp，在 [2, 5] 范围内。\n      论文采用 unfixed 数据并标注 caveat：\"evaluation uses standard train/test split; \n      per-test leakage analysis pending\"。这是 acceptable 但 reviewer 可能质疑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek func-level three-format comparison (CLS / CWM / TRAJ)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      使用现有 deepseek-traj-func-v2 数据，CLS>TRAJ gap (3.69pp) 作为 suggestive evidence。\n      Seed123: CLS 86.77% vs TRAJ 85.08% = 1.69pp gap。\n      Mean gap: ~2.7pp，在 median 档 [2,5] 范围内但偏下限。\n      论文措辞：\"DeepSeek func-level results suggest CLS≥TRAJ (mean gap 2.7pp, N=2 seeds), \n      though insufficient seeds preclude formal equivalence/superiority testing\"。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-s123-fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"deepseek-traj-func-v2-s123-fixed\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek func TRAJ seed123 修复版\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"FAILED_TO_RESOLVE\"\n      reason: \"同 v2-fixed\"\n      fallback_accuracy: 0.8508\n      cls_traj_gap_s123_pp: 1.69  # 86.77 - 85.08\n    result_rationale: >\n      同上。Seed123 unfixed 数据表明 gap 更小 (1.69pp)，增加了结论的不确定性。\n      两个 seed 的 gap 差异 (3.69 vs 1.69) 暗示高方差，进一步支撑 median 档\n      \"仅作 suggestive evidence\" 的定位。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"纳入 seed123 unfixed 数据后 mean gap 降至 2.7pp，方差较大。\"\n```\n\n**关键 median 档叙事总结**：\n\n- **C1**：Qwen 8B CLS-CWM gap = 2.81pp (已验证)；DeepSeek repo gap ~11.4pp 方向一致但因 architecture 差异 CWM parseability 更好，gap 缩小。论文弱化为 \"advantage magnitude modulated by architecture\"。\n- **C2**：仅 Qwen 5-seed TOST p=0.007 standalone。DeepSeek func CLS≥TRAJ (mean 2.7pp) 作为 suggestive evidence，repo-level 缺失。\n- **C3**：不受影响（纯 oracle 分析，model-agnostic）。\n- **Re-repair**：negative，列为 future work。\n- **Critical reviewer concerns**：3/4 addressed（addressed: novelty via scaling + cross-model direction; generalization via DeepSeek secondary evidence; per-test utility via oracle analysis。NOT addressed: downstream impact 仅有 phase0 negative）。","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e2d7180c-b21d-4a12-a938-cc2a4c8f76d9","total_cost_usd":0.42586725000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31771,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"output_tokens":7784,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31771,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7784,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31771,"cache_creation":{"eph